{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>To cause the belly to swell.</b> Like לְהַצְבּוֹת בֶּטֶן — this is the usage of patach, where the lamed has a vowel. So too ״לַנְחֹתָם הַדֶּרֶךְ״ (Exodus 13), ״לַרְאֹתְכֶם בַּדֶּרֶךְ אֲשֶׁר תֵּלְכוּ בָהּ״ (Deuteronomy 1), and likewise ״לַנְפִּל יָרֵךְ״ — לְהַנְפִּיל יָרֵךְ: the waters swell the belly and drop the thigh." "<b>To cause the belly to swell and to drop the thigh.</b> The belly and thigh of the one who had relations with her — or is it not rather the one who was had relations with? When it says ״אֶת יְרֵכֵךְ נֹפֶלֶת וְאֶת בִּטְנֵךְ צָבָה״ — behold, the one had relations with is stated (Sotah 28)." "<b>Amen, amen.</b> Acceptance of the oath — amen on the curse, amen on the oath; amen if by this man, amen if by another man; amen that I did not stray: betrothed and married, awaiting yibbum, and secluded (Sotah 18)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:36.512275437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}